-- הסכם קיבוצי כללי מיום 23.9.2024 — שינוי מבנה שבוע העבודה בחטיבות
-- העליונות: the general collective agreement between the local authorities
-- (the Centre of Local Government, the three large cities and the Centre of
-- Regional Government) and ארגון המורים, registered on 9.3.2025 (no.
-- 7038/2024), for the period to 31.8.2028: a one-time grant for תשפ"ד, the
-- new work week (38 hours) and its tables, shekel and percentage
-- supplements, role rewards, school roles, flexible matriculation and
-- academisation, managers' pay, retirement grants, the union's funds, the
-- day of preparation, the strike days, and exhaustion, industrial peace
-- and the follow-up committee.
--
-- Circular תשפ"ה/5 publishes the agreement for the owners' high schools,
-- §§1–38 nearly row for row (its §38 is this agreement's §43), and its
-- rules were encoded there first (l4/circulars/2024-25_tashpah_05.l4). So
-- each row the two print in the same or nearly the same words is cited "as
-- in circular תשפ"ה/5", by the rule that encodes it there, and this file
-- imports the circular; a row the circular breaks into paragraphs of its
-- own is cited at the paragraph that holds it. What the circular leaves out
-- is encoded here: the preamble, two paragraphs of §14, §§39–42 and 44–50,
-- and annexes ד–ו, the managers' minimum amounts, which the circular names
-- and does not print (its `the minimum amount` takes them as an input).
-- Annexes א–ג, the work-week tables, are illegible in the scan.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT parties
IMPORT conventions
IMPORT vocabulary
IMPORT `2024-25_tashpah_05`
IMPORT minimum_wage_law

§ `הסכם קיבוצי כללי מיום 23.9.2024 — שינוי מבנה שבוע העבודה בחטיבות העליונות`

-- not weighed against `the Equal Opportunities Law`: §8(ג) puts annex ב'
-- in place of the Oz agreement's annex א', the mother teachers' week, as
-- circular תשפ"ה/5 does; the mother teacher is the one the earlier
-- agreements define (§11(ג) keeps their definition), the base agreement's
-- §7(ג) and the takanon's §1.13.1, and the fathers it leaves out of §4(א)
-- are weighed there, on the card mother-position-fathers
-- (F-ofek-hadash-base-7-c, F-1.13-e).

-- The Women's Work Law (through circular תשפ"ה/5): §5(ה)–(ו) count the
-- birth and parenthood period toward the grant at the position on its eve;
-- §34(ג) changes the achievement grant's period, not that; and §42's
-- teacher in the period on the make-up days makes up the strike hours
-- after her return, as circular תשפ"ה/5 does. The floor is met.
`as in circular תשפ"ה/5, §5 counts the birth and parenthood period toward the grant` MEANS
    `§5 of תשפ"ה/5 counts the birth and parenthood period, as the Women's Work Law keeps it`
#ASSERT `as in circular תשפ"ה/5, §5 counts the birth and parenthood period toward the grant`

§§ `המבוא`

