-- The minimum amount annexes ד–ו give, for the post, the classes and the
-- seniority in management: the input the circular's `the minimum amount`
-- takes (`annex ד's amount for the post, classes and seniority`); NOTHING
-- where the table leaves the cell empty.
GIVEN `the cells` IS A LIST OF `managers' minimum of 23.9.2024`
      classes IS A NUMBER
      seniority IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the managers' minimum of 23.9.2024 in` `the cells` classes seniority IS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN c YIELD c's `its classes, 23.9.2024` EQUALS classes AND c's `its seniority in management, 23.9.2024` EQUALS seniority) `the cells`
    WHEN c FOLLOWED BY rest THEN JUST (c's `its amount, 23.9.2024`)
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING

#ASSERT `the managers' minimum of 23.9.2024 in` `the minimum amounts of annex ד' of 23.9.2024` 32 16 EQUALS JUST 30000
#ASSERT `the managers' minimum of 23.9.2024 in` `the minimum amounts of annex ד' of 23.9.2024` 32 1 EQUALS JUST 24000
#ASSERT `the managers' minimum of 23.9.2024 in` `the minimum amounts of annex ד' of 23.9.2024` 1 1 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the managers' minimum of 23.9.2024 in` `the minimum amounts of annex ה' of 23.9.2024` 32 1 EQUALS JUST 19200
#ASSERT `the managers' minimum of 23.9.2024 in` `the minimum amounts of annex ו' of 23.9.2024` 32 2 EQUALS JUST 20910
